<p>Use this menu to adjust the standard settings that can affect the output 
 quality of the print jobs.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="aiqc" role="heading">Adjust Image Quality/Color</p>
<p>Correct the image quality and color tone to make the optimum setting 
 for printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Standard Settings</span></p>
<p>Select the type of your document to print it with optimal settings for 
 the type.</p>
<p>The available items vary depending on the printer you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Generic Documents</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints with settings suitable for a standard document, 
 such as that generated by a wordprocessor or spreadsheet application.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints with settings suitable for documents containing 
 fine gradations in tone, such as photographs.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Depending on 
 the application you are using, images and graphics might be printed in 
 full color (CMYK), even in black and white documents. </p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">DTP</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints with settings suited to reproduction of graphics.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Depending on 
 the application you are using, images and graphics might be printed in 
 full color (CMYK), even in black and white documents.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">POP Display</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the color red more vividly. It is an optimal 
 setting for the POP display.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">CAD</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances reproduction of fine colored lines, for 
 example, when printing from CAD applications are performed.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Settings</span></p>
<p>Allows you to configure the image quality and color tone manually.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span></p>
<p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">Details</span> dialog box and set the 
 details.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="resolution" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span></p>
<p>Select a resolution. The higher resolution will result in better print 
 quality but may cause printing to take longer.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Resolutions are listed in reverse order of quality 
 (lowest first).</p></li>
<li><p>If you print large-sized or high-resolution images, 
 the printing might not be processed due to low memory. In this case, select 
 a lower print resolution than the one you selected.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="tonersave" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Toner Saving:</span> </p>
<p>Select a toner saving mode.</p>
<p>The available items vary depending on the printer you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Off</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints without toner saving mode.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">On</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Reduces the amount of toner used when printing is 
 performed.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Toner Saving 1</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Reduces the amount of toner used when printing is 
 performed.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Toner Saving 2</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Further reduces the amount of toner used when printing 
 is performed (more reduced than when <span class="Term-Soft">Toner Saving 
 1</span> is selected). While this increases the life of the toner cartridge, 
 the output appears slightly lighter.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Medium Light</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Reduces the amount of toner used when printing is 
 performed.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Light</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Further reduces the amount of toner used when printing 
 is performed (more reduced than when <span class="Term-Soft">Medium Light</span> 
 is selected). While this increases the life of the toner cartridge, the 
 output appears slightly lighter.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">User Setting</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Allows you to make detailed settings in the <span class="Term-Soft">Toner Save User Settings</span> dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cud" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free Color Management:</span></p>
<p>Specify whether to convert the colors used in documents to the barrier-free 
 colors applicable to Color Universal Design (CUD).</p>
<p>The color tone of the print result might differ considerably from the 
 color tone of the original.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="priority" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print Priority:</span></p>
<p>Select the method you want to use for rendering bitmaps. When documents 
 containing high resolution bitmap images are printed, printing takes longer 
 due to the large amount of data that must be processed.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Normal</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints with a balance of quality and speed.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Quality</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints with quality as priority.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Speed</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Printing is fast.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">High Speed</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints with the priority on print speed.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="twocolor" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Two-color:</span></p>
<p>Prints in two colors.</p>
<p>Select the combination of toner colors.</p>
<p>This function is available only if <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Settings</span> 
 is selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span>.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/RPCS/IDH_HOW_TWOCOLOR">Printing in Two Colors</a></p>
